cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in work that leads to a publication, please cite it, and cite the original method papers listed in `references` below."
title: "exoklip: KLIP/ADI post-processing for direct imaging of exoplanets"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-light Python implementation of Angular Differential Imaging and
  Karhunen-Loeve Image Projection for high-contrast direct imaging, including
  small-sample detection statistics, throughput-corrected contrast curves, the
  negative fake companion technique, and a Fourier-optics ADI sequence simulator.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Barge
    given-names: François
    alias: francoisbarge8
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/francoisbarge8/exoklip"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - exoplanets
  - direct-imaging
  - high-contrast-imaging
  - angular-differential-imaging
  - KLIP
  - principal-component-analysis
  - adaptive-optics

